<LegalLayout title="Technical Due Diligence — Dawid Golebiewski" description="Technical due diligence for AI, data, and workflow-heavy businesses: architecture review, delivery risk assessment, and operational reality checks.">
  <section class="legal-copy">
    <h1>Technical Due Diligence</h1>
    <p>Technical due diligence is most useful when the surface story sounds convincing, but the operating reality is still unclear.</p>
    <p>I help founders, buyers, and operating stakeholders inspect delivery risk in AI, data, and workflow-heavy businesses: architecture quality, team operating model, context quality, hidden process debt, and whether the claimed automation or AI advantage is actually durable.</p>
    <p>The goal is not a generic traffic-light report. The goal is to identify what can be trusted, what still needs verification, and which technical or operational liabilities are likely to matter after the transaction or investment decision.</p>
    <p>If that is the problem you are solving, the fastest path is still to start the conversation from the homepage and outline the business context, timeline, and the parts of the system that are hardest to inspect.</p>
  </section>
</LegalLayout>
